# GPU heap 0 at the Native cap (LIF-4, SHD-1): the CLI host at 3324x2494, the largest 4:3 picture DM_SCR_MAX_PX (3840 x 2160 pixels) allows and
# the tightest shape measured (2026-11-03: 3840x2880 crashed at the run entry, 3504x2628 left a 3 MiB gap, 3840x2400 a 14 MiB one), on the
# product's interface path for screens narrower than 16:9 (DM_UI_169=1 DM_UI_YPOS=bottom: 3324x1870 in the front end, 3324x2494 in a run), with
# 3D 100%, Ultra shadows and environment shadows. In game the anti-aliasing mode byte is switched SMAA -> FXAA -> SMAA through the control port
# (SMAA's targets are made on first use), then the run is left and entered again (the 16:9 <-> 4:3 switch rebuilds the display textures). The
# gpuheap events (dm_gpuheap.c) record heap 0 after each change: pool_mb=768 is the positive control (the rewriter's budget); the largest free gap
# is the room the next rebuild has, and dm_gpuheap.c logs a red line when it falls under 64 MiB (measured: 76 MiB at the smallest). Another size:
# --env DM_GAME_RES=<w>x<h>. It departs from this Mac's Recommended because only DM_GAME_RES renders a size this display cannot show; heap
# readings are measurements, so it runs in front and in real full screen (DM_TEST_FULLSCREEN_AT). Run it alone (about 3 GB of GPU memory).
name heap0_cap
requires cli
front fullscreen
save warlock
timeout 400
env DM_GAME_RES=3324x2494 DM_UI_169=1 DM_UI_YPOS=bottom DM_3D_SCALE=1.0 DM_SHADOW_SIZE=4096 DM_ENV_SHADOWS=1 DM_AA_MODE=off DM_TEST_FULLSCREEN_AT=1

expect main_menu timeout=150
enter_game
sleep 3
mem main+0x31e0848 1 chain=0x6614 write=02
sleep 3
mem main+0x31e0848 1 chain=0x6614 write=01
sleep 2
mem main+0x31e0848 1 chain=0x6614 write=02
sleep 3
open_pause
press A
expect game_leave timeout=30
expect main_menu timeout=60
enter_game
sleep 3
quit
check no_red
check no_red_log
check event gpuheap pool_mb=768
